<div class="tale-introduction"><p class="eyebrow">THE GODDESS REMEMBERED</p><p>This original English retelling follows the <strong>Devi Mahatmya, chapters 5–11</strong>, within the Markandeya Purana. It traces a single narrative arc from the gods’ remembrance of the Goddess to the defeat of Shumbha. Battle catalogues and graphic details are condensed, while the sequence of manifestations is preserved.</p></div>
<section class="story-characters" aria-labelledby="characters-title"><p class="eyebrow">MEET THE CHARACTERS</p><h2 id="characters-title">Characters and forms in this story</h2><dl><div><dt>Ambika · Chandika · Kaushiki</dt><dd>Names used for the Goddess who answers the gods and confronts the asura rulers.</dd></div><div><dt>Kali · Chamunda</dt><dd>The fierce Goddess who emerges from Ambika and defeats Chanda and Munda.</dd></div><div><dt>The divine energies</dt><dd>Brahmani, Maheshvari, Kaumari, Vaishnavi, Varahi, Narasimhi and Aindri manifest for the battle.</dd></div><div><dt>Shumbha and Nishumbha</dt><dd>Asura brothers who have taken the gods’ authority and treasures.</dd></div><div><dt>Chanda and Munda</dt><dd>Commanders who first report the radiant Goddess to Shumbha.</dd></div><div><dt>Raktabija</dt><dd>An asura whose spilled blood produces new warriors like himself.</dd></div></dl></section>
